.TH CONDUCTOR-HELPER 8 "2026-10-03" "Samba Conductor" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
conductor-helper \- privileged local helper of Samba Conductor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B conductor-helper
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B conductor-helper
is the only part of Samba Conductor that runs as root. It listens on a Unix
socket that only the
.B conductor
user may use (checked with SO_PEERCRED) and performs a small allowlist of
typed samba-tool operations on the domain controller. When backups are
enabled in
.IR /etc/conductor/helper.toml ,
it also serves conductor-backup on a second socket. It is started by
.BR conductor-helper.service ,
whose sandbox limits it to Samba's state directories and loopback.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-socket " PATH"
Socket for conductor (default
.IR /run/conductor-helper/helper.sock ).
.TP
.BI \-allow-user " USER"
The only user allowed to connect (default
.BR conductor ).
.TP
.BI \-samba-tool " PATH"
samba-tool binary (default
.IR /usr/bin/samba-tool ).
.TP
.BI \-config " FILE"
Optional configuration that enables backups (default
.IR /etc/conductor/helper.toml ).
.TP
.BI \-backup-socket " PATH"
Socket for conductor-backup (default
.IR /run/conductor-helper/backup.sock ).
.TP
.B \-version
Print the version.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR conductor (8),
.BR conductor-backup (8)
